# rule.forbid.verbatim-quotes-outside-seeds

> a wisher's verbatim words live in ONE artifact: their seed. every other artifact (brief, rule, invariant, yield, fulcrum, `.reason`, commit body, PR) states the claim in its own words: no quote, no seed-path citation.

the ban covers the CITATION: a seed path is phantom once published, rots, and frames a law as a report of an utterance. a law carries why it holds, never who spoke it.

```md
👎  > *"only urgent concessions…"* — the wisher (seed S14)
👎  the wisher set the line at shipped harm. ⇒ `$route/.seeds/…S14…md`
👍  the line sits at shipped harm: only an `urgent` concession earns more budget.
```

| when… | then… |
|---|---|
| you would paste `> *"…"*` attributed to the wisher | state the claim, and stop |
| you would soften it to a seed path | same defect, one hop out |
| you write *"the wisher said"* / *"verbatim"* | cut the attribution |
| the quote is "sharper than any restatement" | write the sharper restatement |
| you cannot find the seed | archive it first, then still do not cite it |

not a violation: the seed's own `.said` · a seed cited from within its own route · a published external source · a reviewer concern in a `.taken`.

extant copies: fix forward on contact; no bulk find-and-replace.

blocker: a wisher utterance reproduced outside its seed · a seed path cited from a brief, rule, invariant, or philosophy · *"the wisher said X"* as a claim's ground · a bulk rewrite.
